# Current repository context service v1

`repository_context_v1.py` enrolls a declared complete public source inventory,
captures its current bytes and Git executable status, and invokes the frozen native
producer and consumer in separate subprocesses. A new preparation directory is
required for every source or objective revision. It never executes repository code
or invokes a provider. Every raw file remains available, including unresolved and
opaque dependencies; symlinks are retained as opaque metadata and never followed.

The request example is `repository_service_qualification_v1/request.json`. Its
closed schema contains task/repository identities, an absolute current source root,
the complete public path list, target paths, public objective title/text/authority,
and provenance. The path list is caller authority: undeclared file contents are
never read. Inventory mismatch rejects the preparation. The root `.git` entry is
excluded; other unlisted files require explicit public enrollment. Only ordinary
files and opaque symlinks are admitted. This is a quiescent workspace profile,
with current-source checks before and after operations, not an atomic concurrent
filesystem snapshot service.

```sh
/usr/bin/python3 -B repository_context_v1.py prepare \
  --request /absolute/public_request.json \
  --profile /absolute/runtime_source_manifest.json \
  --run /absolute/new_run

/usr/bin/python3 -B repository_context_v1.py read \
  --run /absolute/new_run \
  --expected-request-sha256 REQUEST_HASH \
  --expected-freeze-sha256 FREEZE_HASH \
  --path package/target.py
```

Preparation returns a summary and binds source, objective, policy, environment,
runtime source files, adapter bytes and the native pack. Its fixed per-process
bound is 600 seconds; errors preserve logs and an incomplete outcome. Reads return
the public objective and requested source bodies as base64, with hashes and the
native pack CID. They check caller request/freeze identities, every runtime source
hash, current original inventory/bytes/executable status/link targets, and the
native source-preserving expansion. All source bundles and members are reverified
by that expansion. The unchanged frozen native consumer's missing required-source
mapping check remains covered by the explicit caller guard.

The native minimal pack is descriptive unsigned context. Its built-in sufficiency
flag and fixed token costs confer no execution, omission, proof-reuse or token
measurement authority. All reads report `execution_reuse_authorized: false`.
There is no signed receipt, published current root, repository repair evaluation,
or provider call in this service.

`repository_service_qualification_v1/qualification.json` records three actual full
16-file XML native preparations: baseline, authored source-comment revision, and
public-objective revision. The twelve checks pass: exact raw bytes; rejection of
source, added-file, executable-status, request and freeze drift; changed source
changes native state/root/pack; objective-only revision keeps state/root and changes
the pack. Each native consumer also performs the existing eleven admission and
tampering controls. The original source copy was restored. A first driver control
incorrectly toggled only one executable bit; its preserved record explains why
that did not change Git executable status. The corrected control toggles all bits.

This is an existing exposed development repository, with locally authored control
mutations. The generic CLI is available. The separately retained five earlier full
Pyparsing producer profiles hit their process deadline. The later explicit
immutable-state profile completes the full native Pyparsing producer/consumer
roundtrip; `REPORT_V12.md` reports its scope, controls and 569.609/1.740-second
process costs. A caller must freeze any successor runtime profile and prepare a
new pack; old Requests enrollments retain their original profile. These context
qualifications are not a complete repair caller or a multi-step trajectory
quality/token evaluation.
